<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Alash Autonomy</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1920 CE · capital Semey</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Kazakh national government of the Alash party, which sought autonomy during the Russian Civil War and whose leaders were later killed in Stalin's purges.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alash-party">Alash</a> party was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakh</a> intellectuals including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alikhan-bukeikhanov">Alikhan Bukeikhanov</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akhmet-baitursynov">Akhmet Baitursynov</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirzhakip-dulatov">Mirzhakip Dulatov</a>. In December 1917 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-all-kazakh-congress">Second All-Kazakh Congress</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orenburg">Orenburg</a> proclaimed the Alash Autonomy and formed a government, the Alash Orda.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alash-party">Alash</a> Orda, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alikhan-bukeikhanov">Bukeikhanov</a>, sought a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakh</a> autonomy within a democratic Russian federation and governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semey">Semey</a> (Semipalatinsk) with an eastern branch, while a western wing operated in Zhympity. It tried to build a militia and promoted Kazakh education and a reformed Arabic script. It allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">Whites</a> at times while negotiating with the Bolsheviks.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Disillusioned with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">Whites</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alash-party">Alash</a> leaders accepted Soviet power in 1919 and 1920, when the government was dissolved and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakh</a> lands became the Kirghiz, later <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kazakh-assr">Kazakh ASSR</a>. Most of its leaders were executed in the purges of the 1930s; they were rehabilitated in the late Soviet period.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/alash-autonomy.jpg" alt="Alash Autonomy" width="320" height="187"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Proposed_Flag_of_the_Alash_Autonomy_(horizontal).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Semey</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alikhan Bukeikhanov</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kazakh</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Alash Orda</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=alash-autonomy" aria-label="Alash Autonomy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6512 426 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Alash Autonomy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6832 682L5635 424M6832 682L5820 533M6832 682L6853 898"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5635 424h0M5820 533h0M6853 898h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6832 682h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6832 682h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Semey. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=alash-autonomy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
